md('LIFECYCLE_MODEL.md','''# Proposed lifecycle — review only

| Layer | What it proves/freezes | What expires or requires requalification | What it does not authorize |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| A. Durable Data Initialization | Certified effective universe, identity/sector masters, qualified accounting/history, source provenance, Level1 disposition/PolicyB, ACTIVE TCX exception, approved policies and tested market capability | A new membership/source/schema/policy/correction may require a new version or incremental initialization; old acceptance stays reproducible as-of its original cutoff | Current market usability, complete M3 score, ranking or capital |
| B. Market Data Readiness | Approved source and transport/manual-ingestion contract, normalization, raw retention, time/identity/adjustments, freshness evaluator, deterministic replay | Credential/provider/schema/calendar/contract changes require requalification; availability monitoring is separate from historical capability proof | A proof that today's market snapshot exists or is fresh |
| C. Analysis-time Market Refresh | Request coverage, trusted analysis cutoff, accepted immutable raw-backed observations and contemporaneous eligibility proof | New required session, expiry, source revision, corporate action or dependency mismatch blocks reuse | DecisionReady by itself; qualitative/valuation/risk gates still apply |
| D. Decision Snapshot | Universe/fundamental/market/portfolio versions, policy/model/engine versions, input hashes, freshness proof and owner exceptions at decision time | New live action requires new eligibility/currentness checks; frozen historical decision remains replayable | Trading on old evidence merely because a past decision was accepted |

**Data Initialization → Market Data Refresh → Analysis → Portfolio Snapshot → Decision → Decision Snapshot.**

This is the logical order. A decision is a candidate until the final decision envelope is sealed atomically with publication; a failed seal must not leave an actionable unbound output. Portfolio snapshot uses the frozen market batch (including held but not ranking-eligible names) and a current ledger watermark. If ledger/reference/market context changes between stages, block and rebuild the affected context; never mutate ledger accounting during market refresh.

The existing implementation already contains pieces of this separation: current read model checks `validThrough < now`; evidence validation checks run as-of; snapshot and decision bodies retain partial lineage. It does not yet expose a separate durable initialization certificate plus accepted first-class market snapshot contract. A dated old acceptance does not literally expire in the existing immutable snapshot code merely because wall-clock time advances. The current release has failed acceptance, not a formerly accepted DI certificate automatically revoked by natural aging.

Legacy ranking currently requires all30 scorecards. An approved prospective PolicyB-aware route must represent full30 identities plus eligible29 and explicit MBB exclusion; a fresh market snapshot alone does not fix that compatibility boundary. Do not invent a score for MBB or silently shrink the legacy route.

The candidate formula needs changes: AnalysisReady also requires all existing applicable financial-cycle, qualitative, valuation, confidence and model gates. DecisionReady additionally requires portfolio integrity/currentness, M1/M4/M5 risk and permission gates. Market readiness is necessary for price-dependent outputs, not sufficient for a recommendation. Fundamental-only descriptive calculations may be explicitly scoped separately; they must not masquerade as complete scores/rankings or redistribute missing weights.

Fundamental partition stays FULL30, eligible by fundamentals29, DEFERRED MBB. A holding in MBB may still need a market price for NAV/risk; that does not cure MBB's CAR blocker or allow new capital. Full-universe membership and ranking eligibility are distinct from the request's observation coverage. Flow/technical remains NOT_APPLICABLE_PERMANENT_M3; a separate technical/money-flow request requires its own approved workflow and gate, never new M3 weight.
''')
md('MARKET_DATA_READINESS_PROPOSAL.md','''# Market Data Readiness Contract — PROPOSED, NOT APPROVED

A capability certificate is hash-bound to approved source contract, adapter/normalizer version, provider schema/template identity, security universe/venue coverage, freshness policy, exchange-calendar version, corporate-action rules and a retained validation corpus. It records issuer/provider authority separately from provenance transport. Existing financial APIs do not become authoritative market sources by being available. A controlled manual import can qualify only if the actual market-source evidence and its approved ingestion/retention/replay process qualify; a free-text source URL is insufficient.

| Requirement | Exact proposed minimum | Fail closed when |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Approved sources | Versioned approved source stack, purpose/venue/field allowlist, licensed/authorized capture path, effective/known-at dates, explicit fallback precedence | Source unapproved, wrong purpose or conflict silently resolved by convenience/latest/equal amounts |
| Security identity | Stable securityId plus effective ticker, exchange, instrument/class and currency mappings at observation time | Missing mapping, ticker reuse, cross-ticker contamination or future mapping |
| Price meaning | Explicit close/last/reference/bid/ask/other field, session state, market timezone, observed trading timestamp/date; no field substitutions | Last/ref/adjusted close treated as raw close without approved semantic conversion |
| Adjustments | RAW/ADJUSTED basis, adjustment/factor version and corporate-action knowledge boundary; shares population aligned with market-cap calculations | Mixed raw/adjusted series, unknown split/rights/dividend factors, future-factor leakage |
| Unit/currency | Lossless decimals; declared quote multiplier, currency and volume/share units; explicit conversion formula/rate/time/source | Guessing VND versus thousands VND, share versus lot, missing versus zero |
| Time | Distinct observation/session, publication/provider-receipt, retrieved/ingested, source-revision-known-at and analysis cutoff | Retrieval timestamp is used to freshen old source observations; future receipt/event or unknown required time boundary |
| Provenance/raw | Immutable sanitized request inventory, endpoint/mode/parameters, response status, retrieval time, raw payload path/hash, exact source cell pointer and normalized-to-raw lineage | Normalized rows or hash alone survive but actual required raw bytes/replay equivalent do not |
| Schema/version | Provider schema fingerprint, template/codes/order, adapter and normalizer versions; failed captures quarantined | Schema drift, incompatible field/code changes or rejected cells admitted silently |
| Freshness | Preapproved per-purpose/session/delay policy and exchange calendar; independently recomputable eligible-until and reason per required observation | Missing policy/threshold ownership, UNKNOWN/STALE, unsupported halt/suspension/no-trade handling, unapproved fallback |
| Missing/conflicts | Required coverage plan; zero only when explicitly a valid zero for that field; reasoned no-trade status; typed missing/conflicting observations | Missing price becomes0, missing bar becomes zero volume, partial universe silently becomes complete ranking |
| Corporate actions | Bind effective/known-at adjustment facts and share-count definitions; keep portfolio events/ledger ownership separate | Market refresh rewrites transaction/cash/cost basis or double-counts a corporate action |
| Snapshot/replay | Stable immutable marketSnapshotId/content hash, observation/source membership, transformation/calendar/adjustment/policy pins and deterministic replay | Re-fetching today's values is offered as reproduction of yesterday's snapshot, or mutable latest pointer substitutes for pins |
| Capability qualification | Retained dated real-source sample(s) sufficient for supported source/semantic coverage plus positive/negative/schema-drift/replay tests and independent review | Only mocks/parser tests exist, all real samples were deleted, or source coverage is claimed beyond evidence |

No numeric freshness threshold is invented here. Ownership/effective dates must be approved prospectively. Provider credentials must not enter logs/manifests. Irreplaceable raw market response and final immutable snapshot records are replay dependencies, not disposable OCR/render intermediates. Where retention is unavailable, an explicitly approved equivalent must reproduce exactly; otherwise the source/use case is unsupported. Retaining a historical raw sample proves capability for a version, not freshness for current analysis.

A certificate may be requalified when source/schema/adapter/calendar/rights change. A provider outage creates an operational availability finding; it does not rewrite an old initialization event. Without eligible current observations it still blocks affected live analysis. This review neither certifies the current capability nor fetches any sample.
''')
md('ANALYSIS_TIME_GATE_PROPOSAL.md','''# MARKET_DATA_FRESHNESS_GATE — proposed contract

Apply before valuation, any price-dependent scoring component, ranking/Top10, positive-capital recommendation and any separately approved technical/money-flow analysis. It is a required gate in those workflows, not a dashboard badge. M3's permanent flow/technical exclusion and weights stay unchanged.

Inputs: trusted requestId/purpose/mode and analysisAsOf/knownAt; initialization certificate; effective universe/sector and PolicyB disposition hashes; explicit required-observation/coverage plan; approved market capability/source/freshness/calendar/adjustment versions; immutable marketSnapshotId; exact source/observation/lineage hashes; prerequisite qualitative/valuation/model evidence.

1. Derive the use-case coverage and required session/field/basis from approved policy and trusted clock. Full VN30 ranking must account for all eligible29 and retain MBB as excluded, not silently shrink the denominator. Portfolio valuation includes all held positions even if some are not eligible for ranking/new capital. Declare benchmark/FX inputs when required.
2. Validate initialization certificate/current applicable master and financial-cycle requirements, active exceptions and quarantine. Initialization alone is not analysis permission.
3. Load exact immutable market data and source bytes; validate authority, identity, declared units, time, field/adjustment semantics, conflicts/revisions, coverage and transformation lineage. A hash or normalized number alone is not source evidence.
4. Recompute freshness at the trusted consumption cutoff using the preapproved session/calendar policy. `CURRENT_ANALYSIS` may not supply a past asOf to evade current clock checks. Retrieval today does not make an old trading date current. If a cached snapshot remains eligible and coherent it can be reused; otherwise acquire/validate through the approved refresh path. Refresh failure leaves the gate blocked.
5. Return an immutable gate proof pinning request, purpose, cutoff, input-set hash, observation hash set, policy/calendar versions, eligibleUntil and per-input reasons. Eligibility cannot exceed the earliest mandatory dependency expiry. Status is PASS or BLOCKED with typed reasons; no score0 or neutral fill.
6. Scoring/valuation/ranking consumers assert the exact proof matches their actual data, not a caller-supplied PASS boolean. All existing human/qualitative, valuation, confidence and methodology gates still apply. Check again before publishing an actionable output, DCA/new capital or handing it to execution. Expiry, ledger/reference/source revision or corporate-action mismatch invalidates the live authorization.

Cache key must include purpose/coverage hash, mode/asOf, effective universe, source/schema, calendar/freshness/adjustment policy and source revisions. A cache hit never bypasses recomputation of eligibility. Do not fall back from the latest invalid/unknown quote to an older valid quote silently. No fixed-day allowance is added by this proposal.

For the Oct19→Oct25 example, assume the earlier snapshot is stale under the approved trading-session policy. Initialization remains an auditable historical PASS if actually approved; the new request is BLOCKED until a fresh accepted snapshot exists. On nontrading dates the required session follows the approved calendar, not necessarily the calendar date of the request. Hypothetical dates do not establish a universal six-day threshold.

Historical/backtest mode never invokes a current refresh to fill old gaps. Require historically effective universe/sector, historically available fundamentals/estimates, historical market observations and revision/adjustment/owner-policy knowledge at simulated cutoff. CURRENT_ANALYSIS qualification, later publication, restatements or a later owner exception cannot retroactively create PIT knowledge. Replaying an old decision evaluates its frozen then-current freshness proof, while new live reuse evaluates today's eligibility.

Existing hard-risk alerts/exits must not be hidden by a missing market feed. This proposal grants no execution bypass: price-dependent sizing/execution and any special risk procedure remain subject to their existing M1/M4/M5 contracts. It cannot authorize new capital under stale/missing data.
''')
md('DECISION_SNAPSHOT_PROPOSAL.md','''# Decision Snapshot envelope — proposed vNext

Existing DecisionArtifact/scorecard/portfolio lineage and immutable body hashes are useful foundations; they are not discarded. The new envelope makes the full multi-domain binding explicit and enforceable instead of assuming an opaque source/version string proves market replay.

Freeze at minimum:

| Fields | Required binding |
| --- | --- |
| decisionId, decisionTimestamp, requestId, mode, decisionAsOf, systemKnownAt | Trusted clock and causal ordering; live versus historical/backtest explicit |
| initializationSnapshotId / acceptanceHash | Approved durable initialization manifest and capability certificate version |
| universeSnapshotId, sectorSnapshotId | Effective identity/membership/sector master, including full universe and eligibility/exclusions |
| fundamentalSnapshotId, qualification/disposition/exception hashes | Exact selected accounting facts, periods/scopes, revisions, owner exception ACTIVE for TCX and MBB quarantine; no current qualification manufactured into PIT |
| marketSnapshotId, marketGateProofId/hash | Actual price/volume/required observation set, raw payload/source memberships, semantics/units, session/calendar/adjustment/freshness policies and eligibility at consumption |
| analysisSnapshotId, scorecardId, rankingId where applicable | Actual model evidence and output membership; no rankings generated by this review |
| portfolioSnapshotId, portfolioAsOf, ledgerWatermark, reconciliation, priceVersion | Current quantities/cash/costs and coherent valuation source from the frozen market batch; no market-driven ledger writes |
| policyVersion, PolicyB partition hash, scoringModelVersion, decisionEngineVersion | Full method/software/normalizer/schema hashes and effective/known-at governance records, not human-readable version labels alone |
| source hashes, normalized observation/transform hashes, snapshot content hashes | Stored replay dependencies under approved retention; actual bytes or qualified deterministic equivalent, not SHA-only promises |
| freshness status/proof, assessedAt, eligibleUntil, per-input reasons, unresolved exceptions | Recompute then-current authorization; do not assign a permanent LIVE_READY bit to historical decisions |

The logical lifecycle is Data Initialization → Market Data Refresh → Analysis → Portfolio Snapshot → Decision → Decision Snapshot. Implement a final candidate decision plus atomic snapshot binding/publication: if the seal or any final guard fails, no actionable recommendation is published. Require matching market IDs/bases across score/valuation and portfolio context or an explicit approved alignment; a refreshed quote after analysis normally requires rebuilding affected inputs. A ledger-watermark change requires portfolio recapture and affected decision re-evaluation.

Persist append-only/versioned envelopes with referential/body-hash integrity and enforce completeness in repositories/application commands, including cached-result reads. Do not migrate old accepted decisions into vNext by inventing missing source IDs or data. Legacy artifacts retain their versioned replay path; an unqualified historical raw-source gap remains disclosed. Re-fetching new prices cannot repair a missing historic snapshot.

Proposal of logical entities does not require one physical table per entity. An additive versioned storage design should reuse existing trusted source/import, fundamental/portfolio snapshot and methodology infrastructure where semantics match, and add market/initialization/decision bindings where they do not. No schema migration, new decision or snapshot is performed here.
''')
